      "side": 1,
      "message": "At first glance, I didn\u0027t think this would work with our upgrade process because I thought for a second that we would have a race condition between nodes don\u0027t have the constraint in the manager layers once the foreign keys are dropped.\n\nTurns out that isn\u0027t the case because according to our rolling upgrade documentation, all nodes in the deployment should be running the latest release *before* the contract phase is executed. Which means the constraint should be honored throughout the entire upgrade either in the API or in the DB. But, for a brief period of time we should have the constraint duplicated because we\u0027ll be checking it at the API layer on nodes that have new code, and at the DB layer for the nodes that have the older code.\n\nThat might make a good comment for other reviews or maybe other contributors looking to do something similar?",
